        "CAO (a brand centred on the Nicaraguan and Honduran factories acquired in 2009)",
        "Cohiba [US version] (Dominican-made; a different thing from the Cuban brand)",
        "Partagás [non-Cuban] (moved to the Forged Cigar Company in 2021)",
        "Punch [non-Cuban] (of old Villazon descent; Honduran-made)",
        "Hoyo de Monterrey [non-Cuban] (likewise of old Villazon descent)",
        "La Gloria Cubana (handled by Forged)",
        "Bolívar Cofradia (handled by Forged)",
        "Diesel (handled by Forged)",
        "El Rey del Mundo [non-Cuban] (moved to Forged in 2021)",
        "Alec Bradley (acquired in 2023 for $72.5 million)",
        "Room101 (acquired in June 2022)",
        "Captain Black (pipe-tobacco and small-cigar brand from Lane Limited, acquired 2011)",
        "Balmoral (gained through the 2020 Royal Agio acquisition)",
        "Mac Baren (the pipe-tobacco major acquired in July 2024)"
